fund-csharp/19-ef-core-basics/01-detect-.explanation:
Walk the snapshot in order and compare each value with `object.Equals`, which unboxes and uses each type's own equality (decimal ignores trailing zeros; two nulls are equal):

```csharp
foreach (var (name, before) in original)
{
    if (Equals(before, current[name])) continue;
    if (name == keyProperty) throw new InvalidOperationException(...);
    changed.Add(name);
}
```

Comparing with `==` on the `object?` values would compare references of the boxed values and report every value-type column as modified.

